---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE_NAME } from "../consts.js";
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description={`What ${SITE_NAME} is, where its data comes from, and how it is produced.`}
>
  <div class="static-page">
    <h1>About</h1>

    <p>
      <strong>{SITE_NAME}</strong> publishes short, plain-English news briefs
      about insider transactions at S&P 500 companies. Each brief is built from a
      single <a
        href="https://www.sec.gov/about/forms/form4data.pdf"
        rel="noopener"
        target="_blank">SEC Form 4</a
      > filing — the report a company's officers, directors and large shareholders
      must submit when they buy or sell that company's stock.
    </p>

    <h2>Where the data comes from</h2>
    <p>
      All figures — names, job titles, share counts, prices and dates — are taken
      directly from filings on the public{" "}
      <a href="https://www.sec.gov/edgar" rel="noopener" target="_blank"
        >SEC EDGAR</a
      > system. We do not estimate or fill in missing values; when a filing does not
      report a number, the brief leaves it out.
    </p>

    <h2>How briefs are produced</h2>
    <p>
      The pipeline is automated. Filings are parsed by code, each brief is
      drafted by a language model from the parsed record only, and a second
      automated pass checks every figure back against the filing and blocks
      briefs that add outside facts, speculate about motives, or read as
      investment advice. A mandatory disclaimer is appended to every brief.
    </p>

    <h2>What this site is not</h2>
    <p>
      This is an independent information source. It is <strong
        >not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to</strong
      > the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission or any government agency.
      Nothing here is investment advice, and an insider buying or selling stock
      does not predict how that stock will perform. See our{" "}
      <a href="/terms/">Terms</a>, <a href="/disclosure/">Disclosure</a> and{" "}
      <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      If a brief misstates something in the underlying filing, email{" "}
      <a href="mailto:naka.kn007@gmail.com">naka.kn007@gmail.com</a> with a link
      to the page and we will correct or remove it.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
